export anchor TestSelection:
    description:
        Targets and `--tags` narrow the run together: a test runs when a
        target names it, or there are no targets, and its tags match the
        expression, or there is none. When the selection leaves nothing, the
        run is an error, since a run that tests nothing is never what was
        meant.

        A target is first a test's name, matched exactly. A target that is no
        test's name is a path, relative to the project root or absolute, and
        names every test declared in that file or in a file under that
        directory.
